  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "development",
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "論點明確而且相關：作者說明支持植樹的原因 (降溫、鼓勵步行、長期投資)，例如 \"Trees lower the temperature, so people are more willing to walk or ride a bike instead of driving.\"，有良好支持但可再加具體數據或反駁細節。"
    },
    {
      "id": "organization",
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "結構清晰，段落轉折自然：先承認 Student A，再支持 Student B，最後總結立場，如 \"For these reasons, I believe planting trees is a smarter long-term investment.\"，但論證順序可更緊密連接證據與結論。"
    },
    {
      "id": "languageUse",
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "用詞與句構多樣且適切：使用複合句與因果連接詞如 \"because\", \"on the other hand\"，語言表現成熟，只有少數可以改進的措辭。"
    },
    {
      "id": "accuracy",
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "語法與拼字大致正確，句子清楚流暢，例如 \"streets without shade are almost unbearable to walk on.\"，只有輕微風格或搭配問題，並不影響理解。"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "quote": "streets without shade are almost unbearable to walk on.",
      "type": "sentence",
      "why": "句尾以副詞片語結束雖然可接受，但在正式寫作中可改為更簡潔的被動或名詞片語結構以提升正式度。",
      "suggestion": "streets without shade are almost unbearable to walk along."
    },
    {
      "quote": "Trees lower the temperature, so people are more willing to walk or ride a bike instead of driving.",
      "type": "cohesion",
      "why": "這句有因果關係，但缺乏連接到經濟影響的具體說明；讀者需自行推論為何步行有利商店。",
      "suggestion": "Trees lower the temperature, making walking and biking more comfortable; as a result, more people walk past local shops and stop to browse."
    },
    {
      "quote": "Building more parking, on the other hand, encourages more cars and more traffic, which makes the city hotter and more polluted.",
      "type": "word-choice",
      "why": "此處用 \"hotter\" 描述城市熱島效應可更精確，並可加入短語說明機制以加強說服力。",
      "suggestion": "Building more parking, on the other hand, encourages car use and traffic, which increases heat and air pollution in the city."
    }
  ],
  "more": [
    {
      "quote": "I can see why Student A cares about local businesses, but I agree more with Student B that cities should invest in trees.",
      "type": "tone",
      "why": "開頭語氣禮貌且平衡，但可更直接表明主張以提升立場清晰度。",
      "suggestion": "I understand Student A's point about supporting local businesses, but I strongly agree with Student B that cities should prioritize planting trees."
    },
    {
      "quote": "In my hometown, Kaohsiung, summer temperatures often go above 35 degrees, and streets without shade are almost unbearable to walk on.",
      "type": "punctuation",
      "why": "句中列舉使用逗號連接兩個獨立子句，換成分號或分為兩句會更清晰。",
      "suggestion": "In my hometown, Kaohsiung, summer temperatures often go above 35 degrees; streets without shade are almost unbearable to walk on."
    }
  ],
  "strengths": [
    {
      "quote": "This actually helps shops too, because pedestrians tend to stop and browse more than drivers who are looking for a parking space.",
      "why": "清楚連結植樹與商業利益，論點具有說服力且與題目直接相關。"
    },
    {
      "quote": "For these reasons, I believe planting trees is a smarter long-term investment.",
      "why": "結論明確總結主要論點，表現出良好的論證結構。"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "你的文章論點明確且組織良好，語言使用成熟。接下來可以加強因果連結的具體說明（例如更明確說明為何步行會增加消費），並修正少數句子結構與措辭以提升正式度與精確度。"
}
